{"name":"Sisal","hex":"#c5baa0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sisal","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Central American plant, Agave sisalana, cultivated for its sword-shaped leaves that yield fibers used for rope.","The fibre of the plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sisal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sisal","blocks":[{"text":"Sisal is a species of flowering plant native to southern Mexico, but widely cultivated and naturalized in many other countries. It yields a stiff leaf fiber used in making rope and various other products. The sisal fiber is traditionally used for rope and twine, and has many other uses, including cloth, footwear, hats, bags, carpets, geotextiles, and dartboards. It is also used as fiber reinforcements for composite fiberglass, rubber, and concrete products. Like other agaves, the pith of the leaves can be fermented and distilled to make mezcal."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/Plantsisal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sisal","wikidata":"Q159221"},{"title":"Sisal (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Sisal, acronym for Sport Italia Società a responsabilità limitata, active since 1946, is an Italian gambling company and payment service provider which has a network of around 35,000 payment terminals throughout the country."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Logo_Corporate_Sisal.svg/330px-Logo_Corporate_Sisal.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sisal_(company)","wikidata":"Q3943659"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Agave_sisalana_W_IMG_2378.jpg/250px-Agave_sisalana_W_IMG_2378.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Agave_sisalana_W